The repair is complete and verified. Summary:

## Root cause
The compile gate runs `lake env lean <absolute-path>` with **cwd = the worktree root** (see `longrun/bin/dispatch_loop.py:71`), but this worktree only contained the `release/` Lake package — no root `lakefile.toml`/`lean-toolchain`/manifest/`.lake`. So `lake` fell back to an unconfigured elan default and every file exited 1 with `no default toolchain configured`, before any Lean was elaborated.

## Fix (infrastructure only — no `.lean` source touched)
Mirroring the accepted D9 sibling worktrees (`D9-ancient-kappa-solutions`, `D9-deturck-trick`), I added a worktree-root Lake workspace:
- `lean-toolchain` → `leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2`
- `lakefile.toml` → root workspace requiring mathlib `master`, no Lean libs/sources
- `lake-manifest.json` → copy of `release/lake-manifest.json` (mathlib `7974e751…`)
- `.lake -> release/.lake` → shares the release build artifacts

Then built the authored chain (`Gronwall ← Basic ← MatrixModel ← Statements`) so sibling imports resolve from oleans. The 5 authored files are byte-identical to before (sha256 unchanged).

## Evidence (re-ran the exact gate procedure)
| check | result |
|---|---|
| **full gate**: all 69 `.lean` files, `lake env lean` from worktree root | **69/69 exit 0** (282.1 s total) |
| D9 files (absolute paths, as the gate passes them) | `Gronwall` 5.67 s, `Basic` 5.24 s, `MatrixModel` 5.71 s, `Statements` 5.88 s, `AxiomAudit` 5.75 s — all exit 0 |
| `cd release && lake build` (all default targets) | exit 0, 8951 jobs |
| `lake env lean D6AuditReport.lean` | exit 0, `D6AUDIT VERDICT PASS` (no sorryAx/project axiom/unsafe/native_decide/proof_wanted) |
| forbidden scan, authored D9 files | 5 files, 0 hard, 0 soft |
| `#print axioms` audit | 82/82 declarations, sole cone `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}` |

The only `scan_forbidden` hits in the worktree are the two intentional ones in the pre-existing D6 `negcontrol/NegativeControl.lean` (the scanner's designed negative control).

